# Copy to .env.local and fill in. .env.local is gitignored and must stay that way.

# Railway Postgres. From this shell use the PUBLIC (TCP proxy) string the
# Postgres service shows under Connect; it carries TLS. The app on Railway
# uses the private one instead (${{Postgres.DATABASE_URL}}?sslmode=disable —
# no TLS on the private network); never put the private host here, it does
# not resolve outside Railway.
#
# The driver sets sslmode=require when the URL does not say otherwise: encrypted,
# but the server certificate is not verified. Append ?sslmode=verify-full once
# the provider CA is configured.
# Uncomment and fill in. Leaving it commented keeps the filesystem store.
# CURB_POSTGRES_URL=postgres://postgres:PASSWORD@HOST.proxy.rlwy.net:PORT/railway?sslmode=require

# Optional. Defaults to public.
# CURB_POSTGRES_SCHEMA=public

# Set to 1 if your network's resolver hijacks DNS for the chain RPC hostname
# (symptom: every chain agent reports SOURCE_UNREACHABLE and the TLS error names
# a certificate for some other domain). Resolves over HTTPS to Cloudflare while
# TLS still validates against the real hostname. Not needed on a platform with
# an honest resolver.
# CURB_DNS_OVER_HTTPS=1

# Protects POST /api/tick. Generate: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# The same value goes into the scheduler (GitHub Actions secret CURB_TICK_SECRET).
# Leave unset locally and /api/tick accepts an unauthenticated POST for development; in production (NODE_ENV) an unset secret refuses every request with 503 rather than run open.
# CURB_TICK_SECRET=

# Optional. Narrates yesterday's Gazette lede with Claude, once per closed day.
# The prose passes the same policy gate as every agent; the model may repeat
# the record's figures verbatim and may not add one. Without a key the
# templated lede stands and the page says a narration was not configured.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. A Discord or Slack incoming-webhook URL. After every tick the
# conditions a person should know about — an absent agent, a paused feed, the
# stock-token beacon pointing somewhere new — are compared with the last set
# delivered, and what changed is posted once. Unconfigured is reported in the
# tick response as NOT_CONFIGURED; nothing is assumed to have paged anyone.
# CURB_ALERT_WEBHOOK=

# ── The chain the desk reads ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Robinhood Chain (chain id 4663). Unset, the site and the tools read the public
# node https://rpc.mainnet.chain.robinhood.com — measured: any eth_getLogs width
# with fewer than 10,000 matches, state about ten minutes deep. A provider's
# endpoint (dRPC, Alchemy) goes here with its key; it is never written into a
# record or printed. The operator's tools in contracts/ read this variable from
# the shell (or: node --env-file=../.env.local scripts/<tool>.ts); the site reads
# it on Railway. Before it is set on Railway the endpoint is measured the same
# way (npm run probe:rpc, or node scripts/probe-rpc.ts <url>): a free tier that caps eth_getLogs at a
# few blocks serves the tools but not the tick.
# CURB_RPC_URL=

# ── The position product ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The desk reads Robinhood Chain (CURB_NETWORK); the position product's
# candidate components live on another network. Each profile has its own RPC
# override so one variable cannot point both at the same node.
# CURB_POSITIONS_NETWORK=ethereum-mainnet
# CURB_RPC_URL_ETHEREUM=https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com
# The profile `hardhat-local` (chain id 31337, CURB_RPC_URL_LOCAL) exists for
# the rehearsal in contracts/README.md only. Never set it in production.

# Optional. Ondo's documented API needs an x-api-key; without one the daily
# evidence run records ACCESS_DENIED for the Ondo source, which is the
# finding, not a fault. The example address in their specification is never
# used in its place.
# CURB_ONDO_API_KEY=

# Only from a reviewed deployment record. Absent means NOT_DEPLOYED: no
# series index, no reconciliation, nothing read from a chain for it.
# CURB_SERIES_DEPLOYMENTS={"apple-s1":{"chainId":1,"address":"0x…","components":{"A":"0x…","B":"0x…"},"fromBlock":21000000,"q":{"A":"10000000000000000000","B":"20000000000000000000"},"capLots":"1000"}}

# The credit desk (docs/decisions/TOKEN.md). One record, filled only from
# what was read from the chain after a launch: the token, the desk
# contract, the block it was created in, and a pool the site can read the
# price from. Absent means NOT_CONFIGURED: no rate is quoted, nothing is
# sold, no top-up is indexed. No token exists.
# The launch is decided for Robinhood Chain (chain id 4663): the profile is robinhood-mainnet, read through
# CURB_RPC_URL like the desk. priceSource.kind is uniswap-v2-pair (getReserves / Sync) or uniswap-v3-pool
# (slot0 / Swap); the quote is taken as dollars or priced by a Chainlink feed on the same chain.
# priceSource.fromBlock is the block the pool was created in, read from the chain: a top-up mined before it is
# priced at the head when indexed; without it a top-up the pool has no event for waits for one. priceSource is
# null until the pool exists — the desk runs, its code is verified, top-ups are indexed and wait, unpriced.
# CURB_CREDITS={"network":"robinhood-mainnet","token":"0x…","desk":"0x…","treasury":"0x…","fromBlock":61000000,"priceSource":{"kind":"uniswap-v2-pair","pair":"0x…","fromBlock":61300000,"quote":{"kind":"usd-stable"}}}
